Z||000000||Sootah||10-31-2001||07:17 PM||||Just got off of the phone to a mechanic in my area. $500 for the whole engine install. MAX. He said that he charged that much for an engine swap that was a major pain in the ass and took forever. I'll prolly get it for a lot less cause I plan on helping him out the whole time with my car as well as others. (Want to learn, this = free education) He's even gonna prolly come out here to do the work as well as help me drop the engine out of the SE. Sweeeeet. Still may end up having to buy a rebuilt if the SE's engine doesn't work out (Sitting 3+ years. Don't know its condition), but hey, its worth a shot eh?<P>I'm one of the most cynical, pessimistic people you may ever meet and I find myself getting stoked about this.<P>Well, not pessimistic per say.. I expect the worst, but hope for the best. Leaves for less of a dissapointment when things don't work out. You were expecting it.<P>If a rebuilt becomes necissary, whom should I use? There is Ed Parks, $1200 for a rebuilt 18 month unlimited mileage warranty. Or Nevada Drive Train (something like that) $700-$900 with a 7 year or 70,000 mile warranty. I'm also close to Nevada.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">     <BR><sup><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter</sup>||||reg||1
